    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "hey, i'm seeing a CrashLoopBackOff on one of our microservices in GKE. i've checked the basic pods status but i'm not sure where to look next. here are the last few lines of the logs:\n\n[error] connection refused: failed to connect to database at 10.52.0.4:5432\n[error] retrying in 5s...\n[error] connection refused: failed to connect to database at 10.52.0.4:5432\n\ncan u give me a checklist of what to check to see if this is a resource issue, a liveness/readiness probe thing, or just a bad config?",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "This looks like a classic database connectivity issue, likely a configuration or networking problem rather than a pure resource issue. First, verify that the database service (at 10.52.0.4:5432) is actually running and accessible *from* your GKE pod's network. Second, double-check your Kubernetes configuration, specifically checking environment variables or config maps for the correct database hostname and port to ensure no typos exist. Finally, examine any network policies in your cluster that might be blocking outbound traffic from your microservice to the database IP.",
