    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "the connectivity seems okay on the network side, i can ping the db from another pod in same namespace. i'm starting to wonder if it's a resource thing. should i be looking at limit/request ratios or maybe something with the liveness probes causing the restart loop? what would be the specific commands or metrics to check for that?",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Since basic network connectivity is confirmed, focus on the pod's health and resource constraints. Use `kubectl describe pod <pod-name>` to check the events section for OOMKills (Out of Memory) or scheduling failures, which indicate resource pressure. Furthermore, monitor the pod's CPU and memory usage via `kubectl top pod <pod-name>` during startup to see if it spikes and gets throttled or killed before connecting. If resources are fine, review the `livenessProbe` definition to ensure the health check only runs after the service has finished its initial database connection attempt.",
      "source": "target",
